<title>SWITZERLAND: SWISS NEWSPAPER AD PAGES RISE 3.3 PCT IN APRIL Y/Y.</title>
<headline>SWISS NEWSPAPER AD PAGES RISE 3.3 PCT IN APRIL Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advertising pages in Swiss newspapers rose 3.3 percent in April compared with a year earlier, according to figures compiled by the WEMF media tracking agency.  (pct change in pages vs year-ago)    April    Jan-April</p>
<p> Daily/weekly newspapers		  + 3.3	- 7.1</p>
<p> Commercial ads			     + 4.3	- 4.5</p>
<p>    Employment ads			  - 5.1     - 24.0</p>
<p> Free newspapers			    + 9.3	- 2.2</p>
<p>    Commercial ads			 + 11.0	+ 0.4</p>
<p>    Employment ads			 - 12.6     - 33.0</p>
<p> Magazines				    - 1.3	- 2.8</p>
<p>    Multicolour ads			 + 2.0	+ 0.4</p>
<p>    Black and white ads		  - 11.7     - 11.0</p>
<p> Specialised publications		 + 4.8	- 7.5</p>
<p>    Multicolour ads			+ 28.7	+ 7.2</p>
<p>    Black and white ads		   - 6.2     - 13.3</p>
<p>The Association of Swiss Advertising Companies (VSW) said the figures reflected the fact that April 1997 had two more days than the year-earlier month because of Easter holidays, noting the cumulative data for 1997 were more representative.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
